|image2 =Ornithogalum umbellatum plant.jpg|caption2=Ornithogalum plant|alt2=Entire plant after digging up
|image3 =Ornithogalum umbellatum (Dame de onze heures) 01.JPG|caption3= Clump of scapes with closed flowers arising from basal leaves|alt3=Scapes arising from tuft of leaves 
}}
The [[inflorescence]] bears 6–20 flat star shaped flowers on ascending stems ([[pedicels]]), {{convert|3|-|3.5|cm|abbr=on|frac=4}}, associated with membranaceous leaflets ([[bracts]]), {{convert|2.5|-|3|cm|abbr=on|frac=4}}, in an open branching umbrella ([[umbel]]) shaped terminal cluster, described as a [[Panicle|corymbose]] [[raceme]].{{sfn |Gadella |1972}} The petal-like [[perianth]] is radially symmetric ([[actinomorphic]]), which is {{convert|1.5|-|2|cm|abbr=on|frac=4}} in diameter, consists of six [[lanceolate]] [[tepals]] which are white with a green stripe on the underside (outside), {{convert|15|mm|abbr=on|frac=4}} in length and {{convert|5|mm|abbr=on|frac=4}} wide. From the outside the closed flower appears green with white margins.{{sfn |IPANE |2019}}

The reproductive parts consist of both male ([[androecium]]) and female ([[gynoecium]]) parts ([[Hermaphrodite (botany)|hermaphrodite]]). The androecium has six yellow-brown [[stamens]] that are free of the perianth and form two groups, each of about {{convert|5|-|8|mm|abbr=on|frac=8}}, with filaments that are simple and flattened and oblong anthers that are {{convert|2|-|4|mm|abbr=on|frac=16}}. The gynoecium has a single pistil with a superior (i. e. above the floral parts) [[Ovary (botany)|ovary]] that is ovoid to obovoid, {{convert|3|-|4|mm|abbr=on|frac=16}}, and longer than the [[Style (botany)|style]] that extends above it. The [[fruit]] is a [[capsule (fruit)|capsule]] which is oblong-ovoid with 3 sides and 6 ribs. Within it, each [[locule]] contains many seeds with a black coat of [[phytomelan]].{{sfn |Blamey |Grey-Wilson |1989 |p={{pn|date=October 2020}}}}{{sfn |Jordan |2000}} The species is [[polyploid]] (having more than two sets of [[chromosomes]]).{{sfn |FNA |2003}}

